# What stays out of the published archive.
#
# This file exists for what it does NOT say: the repository's .gitignore
# excludes *.shaderbundle (generated, tied to the Flutter version), and pub
# packages by the gitignore unless a .pubignore overrides it. 0.4.0 shipped
# without the bundle because of exactly that — every hosted consumer failed
# at "No file or variants found for asset" — and this file is the fix: with
# it present, the gitignore no longer decides, and the bundle rides along.
# Run tool/build_shaders.sh before publishing, so what rides is fresh.
#
# The negation is the load-bearing line. A .pubignore replaces only the
# .gitignore of its own directory; the repository ROOT's `*.shaderbundle`
# still applies from above, and only an explicit `!` at this level wins it
# back. 0.4.1 shipped without the bundle for lack of exactly this line.
!*.shaderbundle
build/
.DS_Store
